 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Integrable.lean:68-81 defines `puncturedPhaseSpace` and `mem_puncturedPhaseSpace` with only `[NormedAddCommGroup V]`. Rotation.lean's section declares `variable {V G : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup V] [Group G] [DistribMulAction G V]` and never refers to `Circle` or `\u2102`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Symplectic/Hamiltonian/CentralForce/Rotation.lean",
   "fix": "Move the section `PuncturedPhaseSpace` (all three instances and `coe_smul_puncturedPhaseSpace`) into `CentralForce/Integrable.lean`, right after `mem_puncturedPhaseSpace`. Keep it under the existing `[NormedAddCommGroup V]` variables, before the `[InnerProductSpace \u211d V]` line. `Rotation.lean` then only uses them.",
   "issue": "The `MulAction G (puncturedPhaseSpace V)`, `ContMDiffSMul` and `ContMDiffConstSMul` instances and `coe_smul_puncturedPhaseSpace` hold for any group acting linearly on any normed `V`. They have nothing to do with rotations or `\u2102`, but they live in `Rotation.lean`. Any consumer that imports `puncturedPhaseSpace` from `Integrable.lean` silently lacks the action, which is the instance-discoverability risk.",
   "line": 168
  }
 ],
